WEBVTT

00:03.920 --> 00:04.240
Okay.

00:04.240 --> 00:06.680
So now let's check quickly the syntax of those two methods.

00:06.680 --> 00:08.280
The first one is create insert.

00:08.280 --> 00:11.960
So first step we have to go and create a table using DDL statements.

00:11.960 --> 00:13.880
So we use the command create.

00:13.880 --> 00:17.440
And then we have to tell SQL are we creating a table or view.

00:17.720 --> 00:19.600
In this scenario we are creating a table.

00:19.640 --> 00:21.680
And then we specify the name of the table.

00:21.840 --> 00:23.640
Then after that we have two parentheses.

00:23.640 --> 00:27.960
And inside them we make a list of all columns that we need inside this table.

00:27.960 --> 00:30.400
So we have two columns the id and the name.

00:30.640 --> 00:33.680
And after that we are defining the data type of those columns.

00:33.680 --> 00:35.000
And maybe as well the length.

00:35.000 --> 00:38.040
There are a lot of options that we can add to this syntax.

00:38.040 --> 00:41.280
But now we are just checking the simplest form of creating a table.

00:41.320 --> 00:44.440
Now the next step is that we need an insert statements.

00:44.440 --> 00:49.000
So we are saying insert into our new table the following values.

00:49.000 --> 00:53.200
We are inserting the id number one and the value for the name going to be frank.

00:53.240 --> 00:57.520
So this is a classical way on creating new table and inserting data to it.

00:57.560 --> 01:00.000
Now let's move to the second method, the CTAs.

01:00.200 --> 01:05.800
Now this time we have an SQL query like select from where and some extra logic.

01:05.800 --> 01:07.240
So this is our query.

01:07.520 --> 01:12.240
And then we're going to go and put our query inside edit statements.

01:12.240 --> 01:14.080
It's like we have done it in the views.

01:14.080 --> 01:16.360
It's exactly like we have done it in the views.

01:16.360 --> 01:19.840
But this time instead of saying view we're going to say table.

01:19.840 --> 01:25.540
So again we have the create command and we are creating a table, then the name of the table.

01:25.540 --> 01:28.420
And then we say as and then we have two parentheses.

01:28.420 --> 01:30.300
And inside them we have our query.

01:30.740 --> 01:32.540
And this is where the name come from.

01:32.700 --> 01:36.620
Create table as select CTAs.

01:36.820 --> 01:38.100
So it is very simple.

01:38.300 --> 01:40.740
In one statement you have everything.

01:40.740 --> 01:42.580
You are creating a new table.

01:42.580 --> 01:47.060
And as well you are inserting the data that comes from this query.

01:47.100 --> 01:52.060
Now this syntax is used in databases like MySQL, Postgres and Oracle.

01:52.100 --> 01:55.900
But in MySQL we have like a shorter way on how to do it.

01:55.940 --> 01:59.300
Again we have our query select from where.

01:59.500 --> 02:05.580
But now in SQL server we can insert a command between the select and from like this.

02:05.580 --> 02:10.980
So we are saying select the following columns into a new table.

02:10.980 --> 02:12.740
So we have this keyword into.

02:12.780 --> 02:14.020
Then the table name.

02:14.020 --> 02:18.340
And then you continue after that with your query from where aggregations and so on.

02:18.340 --> 02:22.220
So here it's like the DDL is inside your query itself.

02:22.220 --> 02:27.860
But in the other databases you can have like the query is separated from the DDL statements.

02:27.900 --> 02:34.020
Personally I prefer this syntax than having this into because if you have like big complex query, this

02:34.020 --> 02:37.460
can be really hard to see and to miss the column selection.

02:37.460 --> 02:40.780
So this is the syntax of creating new table from a query.

02:40.820 --> 02:43.220
The CTAs in different databases.
